title: The idle timer can stop a stdio child in the middle of a call longer than idle_timeout
updated: 2026-11-06T11:47:18Z
---

Found during k26 (drift). The idle timer is armed at a call start, not at its end, so a call that runs longer than idle_timeout can have its child stopped mid-call. Verify first with a test (a call of idle_timeout + 1 s); if confirmed, arm or re-arm the idle countdown when the last call in flight ends, never while one is in flight.

Confirmed on HEAD (idle stop 1 s into a 2 s call; a 4 s call killed by SIGTERM). Fix: Upstream::_forward_p counts requests in flight; _arm_idle_timer arms nothing while any is; finally re-arms. Tests in t/idle.t red on HEAD, green EV/Poll.

